  "title": "A dag-like Res(xor) lower bound for the binary left-pigeon principle",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "For n = 2^l holes with l >= 20, every dag-like Res(xor) refutation of the binary left-pigeon principle with 2n pigeons (hole rows of l + 1 bits) has S lines with 3S + 2n^2(l + 1) >= exp(0.005 k / l^2 - 1), k = floor(n/(64 l^3)), that is exp(Omega(n / log^5 n)); since the n + 1 pigeon principle's clauses are a subset, the same holds for the binary left-pigeon principle LP_{n+1}, whose search problem is PPADS-complete. The proof: Theorem (R) for 2n pigeons; a spare-row space separated by a cube with hole coordinates (Braun's cube-drop lemma and moments); Braun's generic criterion with the density count. Conditional on Braun's preprint arXiv 2609.23015 (Lean-formalized, audited by this program), whose lemmas it cites.",
